# Goal Description
Optimize your current native Firefox installation on Zorin OS so that it opens as fast as it does on CachyOS.

## Background Context
I investigated your system and found you already have some of the best tools installed (like `profile-sync-daemon` and `ananicy-cpp` which are staples of CachyOS), but they aren't working correctly for Firefox! Your Firefox profile is currently located in `~/.config/mozilla`, but `psd` is hardcoded to look for `~/.mozilla`. Because of this, your Firefox profile is still loading from the slower disk instead of your RAM.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Fix Profile-Sync-Daemon (`psd`)
- [NEW] Create a symlink from `~/.config/mozilla` to `~/.mozilla`.
- This simple trick will force `psd` to pick up your Firefox profile and move it into your RAM (tmpfs), making startup incredibly fast.
- I will restart `psd` so it begins managing the profile immediately.

### 2. Vacuum Firefox Databases
- [MODIFY] I will run a script to vacuum (defragment) all the `.sqlite` databases inside your Firefox profile. Over time, these get fragmented and cause slow startup times. Vacuuming them is perfectly safe and highly recommended for speed.

## User Review Required
Are you okay with me applying these optimizations? Since it touches your Firefox profile database, please let me know if you approve before I proceed!

## Verification Plan
### Automated Tests
- Run `psd p` to verify that `psd` successfully detects the Firefox profile in the new symlink path.
- Check database sizes before and after vacuuming.
